// CASE 6 — what does NOT having the marker actually cost?
//
// The error message is not the cost. The question is BLAST RADIUS: one
// unwritten function sits in a module with two finished ones. Does the
// compiler still check and emit the finished two, or does the whole module
// go dark until somebody writes the third?
//
// F15 makes a directory a module, so "the module" here is every .bs file in
// the directory — this is the unit that either compiles or does not.
module StubMixed

type FrameType = :method | :header | :body | :heartbeat

// FINISHED, and exhaustive.
public int Weigh(FrameType f)

Weigh(:method) -> 1
Weigh(:header) -> 2
Weigh(:body) -> 3
Weigh(:heartbeat) -> 0

// FINISHED, and it has a real defect in it: `Label(:body)` returns an int
// where the signature promises a string. If the module compiles, the
// checker should catch this. If it does NOT get caught, then the unwritten
// function below is HIDING it, and the cost of no marker is not one error,
// it is every diagnostic downstream of the first stub.
public string Label(FrameType f)

Label(:method) -> "method"
Label(:header) -> "header"
Label(:body) -> 3
Label(:heartbeat) -> "heartbeat"

// UNWRITTEN. This is the stub.
public int Priority(FrameType f)
